course: dictionary
lesson: 6009
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «meddle» is one of them. Context tells you which meaning you need. Look at what is happening and who is involved.
explain: «People disagree about how much that meddling changed: some say it reached millions, others say it is hard to show it changed many votes.» Here meddling means getting involved in something that is not your business. The clue is that people are arguing about the effect it had on other people.
explain: The second meaning is about touching or fiddling with something you should leave alone, like «don't meddle with the wires». The clue is the thing being touched: wires can be dangerous. The verb changes its form too: meddle, meddles, meddled, meddling.
fact: Meddle means to get involved in someone else's business when you are not wanted, and often make things worse.
fact: «Meddle with» means to touch or fiddle with something you should leave alone, such as wires, gas or medicines.
fact: «Meddle in someone's affairs» means to poke your nose into their private business.
fact: A meddler is someone who keeps interfering in other people's lives, like a nosy neighbour.
fact: «Those meddling kids» is a famous line from the cartoon Scooby-Doo.
exercise: «People disagree about how much that meddling changed.» In this sentence, meddling means | Fiddling with a light switch to turn it on | Sleeping late | Singing loudly in a choir | *Getting involved in other people's business
exercise: A sign says «don't meddle with the wires». What should you do? | *Leave the wires alone | Pull the wires out to see inside | Ask your aunt to fix them | Tie the wires into a knot
exercise: Which word describes someone who keeps poking into other people's lives? | *Meddler | Painter | Sprinter | Gardener
test: «Stop ___ with the medicine cupboard.» Which word fits best? | *Meddling | Greeting | Sleeping | Painting
test: «Yesterday, Sam ___ in his sister's game and lost her place.» Which form of meddle fits? | *meddled | meddle | meddles | meddling
exam: Which meaning fits best when a neighbour keeps asking about your family's money and makes arguments worse? | Touching the wires safely | Helping you carry your shopping | Playing a game with the children | *Meddling, getting involved where they are not wanted
